  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "plastic_toys_reference",
  "label": "Reference to plastic toys as a symbol of childhood messiness",
  "description": "The scattered plastic toys surrounding the child are not just visual clutter; they symbolize the chaos and messiness associated with childhood play. The text 'when your moms plastic' implies that the child's mother is 'plastic' (a term often used to describe something cheap, fake, or lacking in quality), and the child is the result of this 'plastic' upbringing. This is a cultural reference to the idea that children are products of their parents' choices or environments, which is not directly visible in the image but is implied by the text.",
